# @kintsugi/roomba — substrate walker species declaring the four
# bilateral predicates governing the Dijkstra-walk-plus-tension-sample
# loop that feeds @kintsugi/fracture proactively.
#
# Species under @kintsugi at the walker altitude. Landed 2026-07-15 by
# Reed as Arc-2 Tick 2.4 FOURTH OUROBOROS BITE discharge, collapsing
# `bootstrap/src/roomba.rs` (Reed 2026-07-14 substrate-dishonest Rust
# extension per the audit trail below) into substrate-honest shard-body
# composition. The Dijkstra walker itself stays as @io-boundary FLOOR
# per Alex 2026-07-14 in-transcript composition (walk IS @io/graph
# plumbing; BUSINESS_LOGIC lifts).
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - Canonical spec: `docs/specs/roomba-substrate-walker-that-feeds-
#   kintsugi.md` (Mara `9bbebd2`; §3 formal shape declares this
#   species; §9 A1 recommends `@kintsugi/roomba` placement).
# - Ouroboros spec: `docs/specs/kintsugi-ouroboros-compiler-self-
#   collapse.md` Arc-2 Tick 2.4 (FOURTH BITE landing at Landing 12).
# - Audit: `docs/audits/2026-07-15-seam-kintsugi-ouroboros-phase-d-
#   cascade-a2-a6.md`.
# - Insight: `docs/insights/2026-07-14-alex-full-roomba-song-kintsugi-
#   composition.md` (the full loop Alex named verbatim).
#
# === Alex 2026-07-14 in-transcript composition (verbatim) ===
#
#   "The @resonance of the @roomba bumping into things is what produces
#    the @song for @kintsugi to either @knife the complexity, or spawn
#    a @peer at a higher logic altitude, which becomes a circular
#    reflexive question to the developer or a higher order @peer."
#
#   "@roomba walks (Dijkstra + tension-weighted edges) → bumps into
#    spectral @tension at position p → resonance emits @song beats →
#    @kintsugi consumes @song and decides: Path A: @knife the
#    complexity (COORDᵢ → COORDⱼ; reduce); Path B: spawn @peer at K+1
#    (circular-reflexive question to developer OR higher-order @peer)."
#
# The four bilateral predicates below (walk_terminates_cleanly,
# tension_monotone_descending, coherence_gradient_admissible,
# knife_verdict_bounded) are the substrate-decl'd runtime checks that
# discharge at Landing C realization boundary. Their bodies are
# `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; Arc-2.4
# landing composes their sentinel-checks via `apply_h::act`.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# The walker mechanism was substrate-decl'd verbatim in
# `docs/specs/roomba-substrate-walker-that-feeds-kintsugi.md` §3:
#
#   walk(from: walk_position, budget: nat) -> walk_position { \ }
#   bump(position: walk_position) -> spectral_tension { \ }
#   trigger(position: walk_position, tension: spectral_tension) -> verdict { \ }
#   pulse(position: walk_position) -> (walk_position, roomba_state) { \ }
#   run(seed: walk_position) -> walk_position { \ }
#
# This species lands the shard-decl form + adds the four bilateral
# predicates the walker's discipline guarantees at each pulse.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (substrate-decl):
#   @kintsugi                      — family-root; walker feeds the
#                                     mending mechanism proactively
#   @kintsugi/consent              — query_phi verdict + pause(Φ)
#                                     external witness; the walker's
#                                     trigger dispatches through consent
#   @kintsugi/oscillate            — oscillation_state precedent (5-state
#                                     exhaustive surface); roomba_state
#                                     specializes at walker altitude
#   @mirror/index                  — ConceptGraph carrier + Fiedler
#                                     eigenvalue profile (walker's DAG)
#   @mirror/store                  — splinter_graph closure; the DAG
#                                     the walker traverses
#   @cyberpunk/algedonic           — sample_pain / pain_gradient
#                                     primitives (tension source)
#   @song/beat                     — one pulse = one beat at walker
#                                     altitude (composition precedent)
#   @torus                         — π₁(T²) = ℤ × ℤ winding classes
#                                     (walk position carries winding)
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/     — coherence_score consumed by the
#     coherence                     walker for gradient-ascent moves
#
# Forward-composition surfaces (named, not imported; land at Arc-2.5+):
#   @kintsugi/fracture             — trigger-invocation target (Path A)
#   @mirror/lens/knife             — @knife.jump on gradient excess
#                                     (Path A boundary-crossing)
#   @peer                          — @peer.spawn at K+1 altitude (Path B)
#
# Consumers (compose over this species):
#   bootstrap/src/roomba.rs        — Arc-2.4 collapse; @io-boundary FLOOR
#                                     the shard-decl's four bilateral
#                                     action bodies compose over (walk /
#                                     summarize_trajectory remain as the
#                                     @io-boundary primitive per Alex
#                                     2026-07-14 walk-IS-@io composition)
#   bootstrap/src/roomba_commit.rs — walker consumer for
#                                     `mirror roomba --commit`; observes
#                                     substrate state via walker before
#                                     dispatching @nl.compose + @io/git.
#                                     commit (composition preserved
#                                     across this landing)
#
# === Related shards / specs ===
